From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-3-0105: add ordered sparse replay cursor

Make replay cost proportional to intersecting native work instead of the
holder's total source-object count. Normalize the immutable source, native
run, line-leaf, and path-block cursors at the top of each replay iteration,
then jump exact nonintersecting contiguous line leaves in painter order.

The jump unit is construction-validated: a leaf contains only consecutive
native opaque-line commands and cannot cross a canonical object or another
native opcode. Intersecting leaves and all canonical gaps retain the existing
ordered executor and pixel behavior.

Drive cancellation from bounded replay work units instead of skipped source
ordinals. This preserves responsiveness without paying one cancellation or
dispatch decision per culled command. Add structural tests for canonical and
dense barrier boundaries plus replay metrics that expose actual jump count.
